    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d347-a1">

                <pb facs="0451" n="285" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg285"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Inspector General of
                            Customs to the Chinese Secretary of
                            Legation
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-04-04">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 4, 1917</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Dr. Tenney</hi>: With reference to our
                    conversation this morning concerning export of flour I write to say that I have
                    received the following instructions—namely that until further order Shanghai
                    milled flour may be freely exported by foreign merchants, if covered by <hi
                        rendition="#italic">huchao</hi> to be issued by the Shanghai superintendent,
                    in bags not exceeding 50 pounds in weight. <hi rendition="#italic">Huchao</hi>
                    will be issued by the superintendent on payment of $0.40 per bag.</p>
                <p>Yours sincerely,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">J. A. Aglen</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
